his direction. </span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">Please feel free to ask questions!</span> </li> <br><span class=\"underline\">You can use a modal, like <span class=\"strong\">can</span>  or <span class=\"strong\">could</span>:</span> <li><span class=\"italic\">You could visit many of those sites.</span> </li><li><span class=\"italic\">We could go to Buckingham Palace.</span> <br> <br><span class=\"underline\">You can use a Wh-Hw question:</span><li> <span class=\"italic\">Why don't you sign up for another excursion?</span> </li><li><span class=\"italic\">How about going on a tour of Scotland?</span>  <br><br> <span class=\"underline\">You can use the word Let's:</span>  <li> <span class=\"italic\">Let's go to the gift shop.</span> "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hanging"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "suspended from the ceiling"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The word Stonehenge means \"hanging stones.\""}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you visit Stonehenge."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to seem "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to appear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you see how they seem to be hanging in the air?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wheel"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a round circle used in cars, bicycles, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These ancient people did not use the wheel."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "material that comes from the ground"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What kind of stones are they?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "other"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "different"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are at least 900 other places like Stonehenge."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "speck"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a very small piece"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Do you see small specks of blue in the stone?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le08ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le08ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Select an unusual object or a photograph of an unusual object. It can be a small statue, a tool, a piece of equipment, etc."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a presentation about the object. Where does it come from? What is it made of? What is it used for?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes to help you prepare."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your object to your class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Answer questions about it."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write notes to prepare for a presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare a presentation with background facts on an object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the object to my class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I answer questions about the object."}]}], "type": "sena"}